text:
olivia: Noticed a bunch of anchors with spaces/plus signs not resolving after migration. Example: /reference/clients#c++-usage and /guides/auth#OAuth (note the parens) don't jump.

noah: Repro'd. Rendered ids are `c-plus-plus-usage` and `oauth` so old links with `c%2B%2B-usage` or `OAuth` fail.

zara: Is this from URL-encoding differences in the build pipeline? Docusaurus now normalizes to ascii-only and strips punctuation.

olivia: Two approaches: 1) add explicit header ids for the hotspots, 2) add a tiny client-side anchor normalizer that rewrites location.hash on load if it doesn't match an element.

noah: Can you sketch the client-side patch? If it's small we can apply as stopgap while we sweep content.

olivia: Sure  here's what I prototyped:```js
window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
  const h = decodeURIComponent(location.hash || '');
  if (!h) return;
  const nid = h.replace(/^#/, '').replace(/[^a-z0-9\-]/gi, m => {
    if (m === '+') return 'plus';
    return '-';
  }).toLowerCase();
  if (document.getElementById(nid)) {
    location.replace('#' + nid);
  }
});
```
It maps common cases (plus signs, spaces, parens) to the new slug style.

zara: That looks fine as an interim. But we must be careful with SEO and canonical URLs. Also add tests for linkcheck so we don't rely on client-side fixes forever.

noah: Agreed. I opened PR https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/4350 that adds the client-side script in the theme and updates three headings with explicit ids. It also tightens linkcheck to fail on internal anchor mismatches.

docs-ci: Build queued for PR 4350  linkcheck running.

infra-bot: Linkcheck failed: 4 broken internal anchors (now treated as failures). See report: https://ci.redwood.ai/4350/logs/linkcheck.json

olivia: Thanks infra-bot. The report points to 4 remaining pages where old links point to encoded chars. I'll patch those with explicit ids and push.

zara: For the migration doc we should add a small section 'Characters that changed in slugs' listing: + -> plus, & -> and, spaces->-, parentheses removed. Helps contributors.

noah: Merged client-side rewrite and two explicit fixes in PR 4350 (preview: https://deploy-preview-4350--docs.redwood.ai/reference/clients). Anchor jump works on my machine.

docs-ci: Linkcheck now passes with 0 errors, 2 warnings (external). Published preview build id 2026-03-23-11:02.

olivia: I've filed an issue #223 to schedule a sweep to either update all legacy links or canonicalize slugs in config. We should decide Q2.

zara: Thanks. Closing this thread  reopen if you find more weird encoded anchors.
